# Testing and validation

## What exists here

- No root app unit-test / lint config found at mirror time
- OPS health scripts: `server-ops/sc2027/healthcheck-prod.sh`, `healthcheck-staging.sh`
- Public HTTPS checks + VPS-local docker/ollama checks (script assumes host access)

## Order of work

1. Identify existing checks for the change scope
2. Run **lowest-risk** validations first (git/status, path checks, public curls)
3. Do **not** run destructive or privileged host commands without OPS gates
4. Document commands run, pass/fail, skips
5. Do not mark done with failures introduced by the change
6. Separate pre-existing vs introduced failures

## Safe defaults from a laptop / Cloud Agent

```bash
curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://nortiqalab.com/
curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://api.nortiqalab.com/health
curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://n8n.nortiqalab.com/
curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://mcp.nortiqalab.com/
```

Full `healthcheck-prod.sh` may fail off-host (docker/ollama/local console) — classify as environment limitation, not necessarily a code regression.

